                "html": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">Every day is different, with Technologists balancing patient care, scientific knowledge and technical expertise.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">A typical day may include:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">Preparing and administering radiopharmaceuticals.</span></p></li><li><p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">Performing diagnostic imaging examinations.</span></p></li><li><p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">Operating advanced imaging equipment.</span></p></li><li><p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">Processing and analysing imaging data.</span></p></li><li><p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">Monitoring patients during procedures.</span></p></li><li><p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">Working closely with clinicians to support diagnosis and treatment planning.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">The profession combines science, technology, communication and problem-solving, making it one of the most varied and rewarding careers within modern healthcare.</span></p><p></p>",
                "colorRole": "default",
